<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mouseion</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mouseion was a research institution founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> under the early Ptolemaic kings, dedicated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muses">Muses</a>. It housed scholars and scientists supported by the state and was closely linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/library-of-alexandria">Library of Alexandria</a>. It made Alexandria the leading intellectual centre of the Hellenistic world and is a key legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mouseion.jpg" alt="Mouseion" width="309" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Greece)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greek_-_Leaning_Muse,_Probably_Polyhymnia_-_Walters_2390.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
